# Architecture

## State Management — MVIKotlin

Each feature exposes a `Store` through `<feature>/api/store/<Feature>Store.kt` and implements it under `<feature>/impl/domain`:

- `<Feature>StoreFactory` — assembles `Store<Intent, State, Label>` via injected `StoreFactory` (provided by `core/mvikotlin/di/CoreMVIKotlinModule` as `LoggingStoreFactory(DefaultStoreFactory())` via Napier).
- `<Feature>Executor` — extends `BaseExecutor<Intent, Action, State, Message, Label>`. Handles `Intent`s and `Action`s; dispatches `Message`s to the Reducer and publishes `Label`s for one-shot side effects.
- `<Feature>Reducer` — `Reducer<State, Message>`; pure `State.copy(...)`.

`Action` and `Message` sealed types live inside `StoreFactory` as `internal` companions.

### Presentation layer

- `<Feature>ViewModel` extends `BaseViewModel<UiState, UiLabel>` (extends `androidx.lifecycle.ViewModel`, exposes `state: CStateFlow<State>` + `label: CFlow<Label>` for iOS via moko-mvvm).
- `bindAndStart { store.states.mapNotNull(stateMapper::map) bindTo ::acceptState; store.labels.mapNotNull(labelMapper::map) bindTo ::acceptLabel }` in `init`.
- Public callbacks delegate to `store.accept(Intent.X)`.
- `onCleared { store.dispose(); super.onCleared() }` — mandatory. Store does NOT auto-dispose.

### UI layer

- `<Feature>Screen` consumes VM via `koinViewModel<FeatureViewModel>()`.
- `state by vm.state.collectAsState()` + `LaunchedEffect(vm) { vm.label.collect { ... } }`.
- `<Feature>Screen` is thin — collects state and labels, delegates rendering to `<Feature>ScreenDetails`.
- `<Feature>ScreenDetails` renders `ShowStateData(isLoading, isError, ...) { /* content */ }`.
- Sub-views go under `views/` directory.

### Visibility

- `Store`, `Intent`, `State`, `Label` — public.
- `StoreFactory`, `Executor`, `Reducer`, `Action`, `Message` — `internal`.
- Mapper interfaces public, `Impl` classes `internal`.
- `<Feature>ImplModule` (`<feature>/impl/di/`) is the only Koin entry consumed by `MainModule`.

Loading: `Store.State.isLoading: Boolean`. Errors: `Store.State.isError: Boolean`. One-shot effects: `Label`.

### Feature template invariants

`Store.Label`, `UiXLabel`, `UiXLabelMapper(Impl)` are always present — even if the sealed interface is empty. Never remove these empty slots; the next one-shot effect reuses them without scaffolding.

## Koin DI

Core bindings in `:shared:main/di/MainModule.kt`; per-feature in `<feature>/impl/di/<Feature>ImplModule.kt`. `MainModule` aggregates all via `includes(...)`.

- `single<T> { ... }` for datasources, repositories.
- `factory { <Feature>StoreFactory(get(), ...).create() }` to expose a feature Store (StoreFactory is `internal`).
- `viewModelOf(::SomeViewModel)` for view-models.

Binding interfaces to implementations — choose by constructor params:

- **No constructor params** → `singleOf<I>(::Impl)` / `factoryOf<I>(::Impl)` (typed target).
- **Has constructor params** → `single<I> { new(::Impl) }` / `factory<I> { new(::Impl) }`.
- **NEVER** `factoryOf(::Impl) { bind<I>() }` / `singleOf(::Impl) { bind<I>() }` — registers `Impl` as primary key, `I` as secondary → impl leaks into the graph.

Resolve dependencies:
- In classes (repos, StoreFactories, executors, view-models): via **constructor parameters** only. No `get()` inside class bodies.
- In composables: `val vm: RoomsViewModel = koinViewModel()`.
- Avoid `KoinPlatform.getKoin().get()` outside DI modules.

`initKoin(appDeclaration)` is the single entry point (idempotent via `KoinPlatform.getKoinOrNull()` guard). Called from:
- `AndroidApp.onCreate` with `androidContext(this)`.
- iOS `MainViewController` factory inside `ComposeUIViewController(configure = { initKoin() })`.

## Compose Navigation

Type-safe routes based on the `Screen` marker interface in `:shared:core-navigation`.

- `Screen` — empty marker interface.
- Route objects: `@Serializable data object XxxRoute : Screen` (or `data class` for routes with args).
- Per-feature `ScreenApi` in `<feature>/ui/api/Feature<X>ScreenApi.kt`. Strict top-to-bottom order:

```kotlin
@Serializable
data object <X>Route : Screen

fun NavController.navigateTo<X>Screen(
    popUpInclusive: Boolean = true,
    popUpToScreen: Screen? = null,
) {
    navigateOnResumed(<X>Route) {
        launchSingleTop = true
        popUpToScreen?.let { screen -> popUpTo(screen) { inclusive = popUpInclusive } }
    }
}

fun NavGraphBuilder.composable<X>Screen(
    // onNavigateTo<Y>: () -> Unit = {},
) {
    composable<<X>Route> { <X>Screen(/* callbacks */) }
}
```

Route objects live in `ScreenApi.kt`, NOT in `:shared:core-navigation`.

`NavigationUtils` helpers (`navigateOnResumed`, `popBackStackOnResumed`, `CheckNavigationResult`) are for screen-to-screen navigation. **`navigateOnResumed` silently drops calls from modal sheets** (FloatingWindow entry never reaches RESUMED) — navigate directly from sheets without the resumed guard.

## Presentation Layer Discipline

### UiX models are mandatory

Domain types must never reach `@Composable`. Map them to `Ui*` models in `<feature>/presentation/models/` via `Ui*StateMapper` / `Ui*LabelMapper`. Mapper is a pure function (`Store.State → UiXState`) — no suspend, no Repository calls.

### ImmutableList / ImmutableMap only in UiX models

`List<T>` / `Map<K,V>` in domain and `Store.State`. `ImmutableList<T>` / `ImmutableMap<K,V>` only in `Ui*` models (converted in the mapper via `.toImmutableList()`).

### Enum → UiEnum with lazy resource getter

When an enum needs a resource in the UI, declare a `UiX`-enum with a **lazy getter** (NOT a constructor field):

```kotlin
enum class UiUpcomingBucket {
    OVERDUE, TODAY_TOMORROW, THIS_WEEK;
    val title: StringResource get() = when (this) {
        OVERDUE -> MR.strings.upcoming_bucket_overdue
        TODAY_TOMORROW -> MR.strings.upcoming_bucket_today_tomorrow
        THIS_WEEK -> MR.strings.upcoming_bucket_this_week
    }
}
```

Constructor-field MR access triggers static-init on K/N in unit tests → `FileFailedToInitializeException`. Lazy getter defers MR access to actual UI call where the resource bundle is present.

### No mapping in @Composable

`when(domainEnum) -> MR.strings.x` inside a composable is forbidden. Map to UI-enum in presentation; composable reads `item.bucket.title`.

Colors from `ResideTrackTheme.colors.*` cannot be extracted to presentation (composition-scoped) — `when(uiEnum) -> themeColor` is the only legal mapping left in UI, since the domain type is already gone at that point.

### Snackbar strings resolved in presentation

`Ui*LabelMapper` injects `StringConverter`, resolves semantic kind → message String, puts it in `Ui*Label.ShowX(message: String)`. UI only calls `label.message`. No `koinInject<StringConverter>()` in `@Composable`.

Presentation module that needs `MR` or `StringConverter` must add `projects.shared.commonResources` in its `build.gradle.kts` — it is NOT auto-wired to presentation by `kmpFeatureSetup`.

### Mapper never calls Repository

Everything the Mapper needs must be in `Store.State`. If mapper needs an external call, the fix is enriching State in the Executor.

## Build Conventions

Every `:shared:feature-X:{api,impl,presentation,ui}` submodule applies exactly one convention plugin: `alias(libs.plugins.conventionPlugin.kmpFeatureSetup)` (plus `alias(libs.plugins.conventionPlugin.jsonSerialization)` on `:impl` that reads JSON, and `alias(libs.plugins.conventionPlugin.composeMultiplatformSetup)` on `:ui`). Module name must be `api`/`impl`/`presentation`/`ui` — build fails otherwise.

Auto-wired by `kmp-feature-setup` (do **NOT** redeclare in the module's `build.gradle.kts`):

| Submodule | `commonMain` auto-wired |
| --- | --- |
| `api` | `core-domain`, `core-mvikotlin`, compose-compiler plugin |
| `impl` | `core-domain`, `common`, sibling `:api`, `core-mvikotlin` |
| `presentation` | `core-domain`, `common`, sibling `:api`, `core-mvikotlin`, `core-presentation`, `koin.core.viewmodel` (via api()), compose-compiler plugin |
| `ui` | `core-domain`, `common`, sibling `:api`, `core-navigation`, `common-resources`, `common-ui`, `koin.compose.viewmodel`, `moko.resources.compose`, composeBundle (runtime + foundation + ui + material3), sibling `:presentation` |

Notes:
- `:ui` must additionally apply `composeMultiplatformSetup` — `kmpFeatureSetup` does NOT auto-apply it.
- Each module sets its own namespace via `androidLibraryConfig { namespace = "..." }`.
- Apply `kmp-library` only to `:shared:common*` / `:shared:core-*`. Never apply it directly to feature submodules.
- Feature-specific deps (e.g. `immutableCollections`, `datetime`, `compose.icons.core`, `core-rooms`, `core-database`) stay in the module's `build.gradle.kts`.
